# The build context is exactly what the Dockerfile copies: everything is
# excluded, then the inputs are named. A new top-level file or folder (local
# state, scratch, session logs) stays out of the context without an entry
# here. Add a line when the Dockerfile starts copying something new.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!core
!server
!NOTICE
!LICENSE-MIT
!LICENSE-APACHE
# Inside the named folders: build output and local databases.
**/target
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
